---
import MarketingPage from '../layouts/MarketingPage.astro';

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: 'Open-Source Devin Alternative: An Architecture and Evaluation Guide',
  description:
    'An honest guide to evaluating Shiba as an open-source, self-hosted Devin alternative. Compare architecture, approval gates, credential isolation, and real costs.',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Shiba',
    url: 'https://tryshiba.dev',
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Shiba',
    logo: {
      '@type': 'ImageObject',
      url: 'https://tryshiba.dev/assets/mascot/shiba-logo-512.png',
    },
  },
  datePublished: '2026-09-26',
  dateModified: '2026-10-30',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://tryshiba.dev/open-source-devin-alternative/',
  image: 'https://tryshiba.dev/assets/og/shiba-og.png',
};
---

<MarketingPage
  title="Open-Source Devin Alternative: Evaluation Guide — Shiba"
  description="An honest guide to evaluating Shiba as an open-source, self-hosted Devin alternative. Compare architecture, approval gates, credential isolation, and real costs."
  path="/open-source-devin-alternative/"
  type="article"
  publishedTime="2026-09-26T00:00:00Z"
  modifiedTime="2026-10-30T00:00:00Z"
  schema={articleSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Open-Source Devin Alternative', path: '/open-source-devin-alternative/' },
  ]}
>
  <!-- HERO EVALUATION -->
  <section class="shell hero">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--navy)] mb-6 shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
      <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-[var(--navy)] animate-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>EVALUATION GUIDE · ARCHITECTURE &amp; GOVERNANCE</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="manifesto-title text-[var(--ink)]">
      Looking for an <span class="text-[var(--navy)]">open-source Devin alternative</span>?
    </h1>
    <p class="lead text-[var(--ink-2)]">
      Developers evaluating alternatives to Devin typically seek five core capabilities: inspectable source code, flexible model routing, background execution off their laptop, isolated task containers, and human approval before changes merge.
      Here is an honest, architectural guide to evaluating <strong>Shiba</strong> against those requirements.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/princepal9120/shiba" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <span>Inspect Source on GitHub</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="button button-outline" href="/why-shiba/">
        <span>Why I Built Shiba</span>
      </a>
      <a class="button button-outline" href="/waitlist/">
        <span>Join Waitlist &amp; Community</span>
      </a>
      <a class="button button-outline" href="/docs/approval-gates/">
        <span>Approval Gate Architecture</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell">
    <!-- 00: EVALUATION PREMISE -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="bias-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">00 / Ground Rules</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="bias-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Written by the creators of Shiba</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          We build Shiba, so we have an obvious perspective. We do not claim feature parity with Devin or any commercial platform, and this is not a synthetic benchmark. We have not run head-to-head competitive trials, so we make no unsubstantiated claims about relative speed, solve rates, or cost savings.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Instead, this guide outlines the concrete architectural trade-offs: what self-hosting on Cloudflare Workers and Sandbox containers offers, what it requires from an operator, and how to pilot a single bounded task before changing any production workflow.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          An open-source repository under AGPL-3.0 gives you code inspection, deterministic container images, and no per-seat vendor lock-in. It does not provide free model inference or eliminate Cloudflare infrastructure fees.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01: ARCHITECTURAL COMPARISON MATRIX -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="comparison-matrix-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">01 / Comparison</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="comparison-matrix-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Architectural comparison: Hosted SaaS vs. Shiba</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Both tools automate repository tasks, but they operate under fundamentally different ownership models:
        </p>

        <div class="compare-matrix my-8" role="table" aria-label="Comparison between Devin Cloud and Shiba">
          <div class="matrix-head" role="row">
            <span role="columnheader">Evaluation dimension</span>
            <span role="columnheader">Devin Cloud (Hosted SaaS)</span>
            <span role="columnheader">Shiba (Self-Hosted Cloudflare)</span>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="matrix-label">Hosting &amp; Infrastructure</span>
            <span role="cell">Multi-tenant managed cloud hosted on Cognition infrastructure.</span>
            <span role="cell" class="highlight-cell">Runs directly in your own Cloudflare account on Workers and Sandbox containers.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="matrix-label">Source &amp; Licensing</span>
            <span role="cell">Proprietary closed-source commercial product.</span>
            <span role="cell" class="highlight-cell">AGPL-3.0-only inspectable open-source repository.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="matrix-label">Human Approval Control</span>
            <span role="cell">Autonomous loop with chat feedback and post-run pull requests.</span>
            <span role="cell" class="highlight-cell">Structured approval card required before any container boots (needsApproval: true).</span>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="matrix-label">Credential Handling</span>
            <span role="cell">Stored and managed within the hosted SaaS environment.</span>
            <span role="cell" class="highlight-cell">Real API keys and GitHub tokens never enter the container; injected at egress.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="matrix-label">Agent Harness &amp; Models</span>
            <span role="cell">Single proprietary agent and model pipeline.</span>
            <span role="cell" class="highlight-cell">Pluggable catalog: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, or Devin CLI with custom BYOK models.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="matrix-label">Network &amp; Isolation</span>
            <span role="cell">Managed cloud sandbox with outbound internet access.</span>
            <span role="cell" class="highlight-cell">Strict egress allowlist; registry.npmjs.org excluded by default to prevent exfiltration.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="matrix-label">Pricing Model</span>
            <span role="cell">Flat per-seat monthly subscription tiers.</span>
            <span role="cell" class="highlight-cell">Pay-as-you-go Cloudflare infrastructure + model tokens at cost. Zero software seat fees.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02: THE FIVE CRITERIA -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="priorities-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">02 / Decision Factors</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="priorities-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Five factors to evaluate before switching</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Decide which constraint is primary for your team before evaluating any agent:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">01 / Source inspectability</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Can your security and engineering teams audit every line of orchestrator logic, tool definition, and container build script?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">02 / Choice of coding harness</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Can you choose between open-source harnesses like OpenCode or commercial CLI tools like Claude Code and Codex per task?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">03 / Off-laptop cloud execution</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Does execution run on ephemeral cloud containers so your local workstation remains unburdened and responsive?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">04 / Concurrent task isolation</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Does each task get its own isolated filesystem and deterministic container ID to eliminate state bleed between runs?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--navy)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)] md:col-span-2">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--navy)] text-sm mb-2">05 / Explicit pre-execution approval gate</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Can a human engineer inspect the exact repository, branch, and planned tool input before any code is written or container is booted?</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03: AGENT HARNESS CATALOG -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">03 / Agent Catalog</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="agents-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Pick the agent harness for each repository task</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Shiba does not force a single agent architecture. Its Docker base image pins supported CLI harnesses, allowing the orchestrator to delegate work according to the task type:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">Supported Harnesses</h3>
            <ul class="text-[var(--ink-2)] space-y-2 list-disc pl-4">
              <li><code>opencode</code> — default open coding harness using provider-native headless execution.</li>
              <li><code>claude-code</code> — Anthropic CLI, optimized for deep reasoning and Slack/Telegram threads.</li>
              <li><code>codex</code> — OpenAI agent CLI for autonomous code generation.</li>
              <li><code>devin</code> — Devin CLI runner for operators with existing accounts.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">Transparent Credential Reporting</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">
              Gateway-backed agents authenticate through Cloudflare AI Gateway with BYOK credentials that the Worker never stores in plaintext. The dashboard reports configuration status transparently without making assumptions about provider health.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04: THE APPROVAL GATE -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="gate-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">04 / Approval Gate</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="gate-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">A human reviews before compute starts</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Many autonomous tools run unattended loops and notify you after code is committed. Shiba makes human approval a blocking gate. Every request produces a pending approval card:
        </p>

        <div class="p-5 my-6 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)] font-mono text-xs text-[var(--ink-2)] overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed">
          Dashboard · Slack @shiba · Telegram · Webhook<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;└── pending approval card &nbsp;[repo, branch, exact prompt, harness]<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;├── human approves → Durable Object starts isolated Sandbox container<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;│&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── streams terminal logs, unified diff, PR<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── human rejects &nbsp;→ record resolved, zero compute provisioned
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">01 / Exact text execution</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Repository URL, base branch, prompt text, and harness are cryptographically frozen in the approval record. Nothing runs outside that payload.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">02 / Rejection provisions nothing</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Rejecting a task terminates the workflow immediately. No container is spun up, no git clone occurs, and no compute minutes are billed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">03 / Ephemeral approval pointers</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Slack and Telegram interactive buttons carry single-use approval IDs re-validated server-side. Stale notifications cannot trigger runs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--navy)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--navy)] text-sm mb-2">04 / Strict approver allowlists</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Chat webhooks check cryptographic signatures and enforce explicit <code>SLACK_APPROVERS</code> lists. Unauthorized channel members cannot approve tasks.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05: CREDENTIAL ISOLATION -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="creds-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">05 / Security</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="creds-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Credentials remain outside the container</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          <strong>No real provider API key or GitHub token ever enters the execution container.</strong> Egress requests are intercepted by the Cloudflare Worker:
        </p>

        <ul class="text-[var(--ink-2)] space-y-2 list-disc pl-5 my-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li><strong>Model egress:</strong> The container uses dummy credentials. Outbound provider requests are routed through your Cloudflare AI Gateway binding, which attaches the authorized secret header.</li>
          <li><strong>Repository Git transport:</strong> <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> is injected in the Worker via Sandbox HTTPS interception. Tokens never appear in clone URLs, bash environment variables, or container logs.</li>
          <li><strong>Strict outbound network filtering:</strong> Only approved provider hostnames are reachable. <code>registry.npmjs.org</code> is omitted by default to prevent supply-chain exfiltration during autonomous runs.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 06: HOW TO PILOT A BOUNDED TASK -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="bounded-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">06 / Evaluation Pilot</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="bounded-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">How to pilot one bounded task</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Before migrating any active engineering workflow, test Shiba on a single, well-defined bug or refactor:
        </p>

        <div class="p-5 my-6 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--navy)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)] font-mono text-xs text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">
          Example pilot prompt:<br />
          "Fix the duplicate status message emitted after reconnecting. Reproduce by interrupting the connection during delivery and verifying reconnection. Keep existing status labels intact. Run test/delivery.test.ts, inspect git diff, and report any skipped checks."
        </div>

        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Evaluate four concrete measurements from the pilot run:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-[var(--ink-2)] space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-5 my-4 text-xs font-mono">
          <li><strong>Setup friction:</strong> Time required to clone, configure <code>.dev.vars</code>, and start the local environment.</li>
          <li><strong>Human interventions:</strong> Number of manual corrections needed before task completion.</li>
          <li><strong>Verification evidence:</strong> Whether the agent ran tests, reported real exit codes, and generated a clean unified diff.</li>
          <li><strong>Review time:</strong> How quickly a reviewer can assess the PR diff versus writing the change manually.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 07: TOTAL COST OF OWNERSHIP -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="cost-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">07 / Cost Model</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="cost-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">Understanding self-hosted costs</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Self-hosting eliminates vendor per-seat licensing, but introduces three direct infrastructure components:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-8 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">Cloudflare Compute</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Workers, Durable Objects storage, and Sandbox container execution minutes billed directly to your Cloudflare account.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--line-2)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--ink)] text-sm mb-2">Model Inference</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">LLM tokens consumed by the planning Worker and coding harnesses, routed through your AI Gateway credentials at cost.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--navy)] shadow-[2px_2px_0_var(--paper-shadow)]">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[var(--navy)] text-sm mb-2">Review Time</h3>
            <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">Engineering time spent reviewing approval cards and pull request diffs. The approval gate ensures you remain in control.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)] text-sm">
          For detailed pricing mechanics and billing breakdowns, review our <a href="/docs/costs/" class="text-[var(--navy)] underline font-bold">Cost Documentation</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 08: WHEN SHIBA IS A FIT -->
    <section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="micro">08 / Decision</span></div>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2 id="fit-title" class="text-[var(--ink)]">When Shiba is the right fit</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          Shiba is ideal for engineering teams that want autonomous coding capabilities deployed inside their own cloud infrastructure, with mandatory approval before execution and full auditability of every line of code.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-2)]">
          If your priority is a turn-key managed SaaS with zero infrastructure setup, a hosted service like Devin Cloud remains an excellent solution. If your priority is data ownership, model choice, and approval control, Shiba is built for you.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions mt-8">
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/princepal9120/shiba" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span>Clone the Repository</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="button button-outline" href="/why-shiba/">
            <span>Why I Built Shiba</span>
          </a>
          <a class="button button-outline" href="/waitlist/">
            <span>Join the Community</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingPage>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: clamp(64px, 10vw, 128px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
